        "original_id": "84872cf6-6477-517f-8a95-bf02a6b228b8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, Glenn Close, Uma Thurman, Pierre Choderlos de Laclos\n- Films: Mary Reilly, Dangerous Liaisons\n- Publications: British Vogue\n- Works: Les liaisons dangereuses, Les Liaisons dangereuses\n\nFacts:\n- In December 1985 and May 1986, Uma Thurman appeared on the covers of British Vogue.\n- In 1988, Dangerous Liaisons was released as an American historical drama film.\n- In 1988, Dangerous Liaisons was based on Christopher Hampton's play Les liaisons dangereuses.\n- Christopher Hampton's play Les liaisons dangereuses was a theatrical adaptation of the 18th-century French novel Les Liaisons dangereuses by Pierre Choderlos de Laclos.\n- In 1988, Uma Thurman starred in Dangerous Liaisons.\n- Stephen Frears directed Dangerous Liaisons, Christopher Hampton wrote it, and John Malkovich and Glenn Close acted in it.\n- Mary Reilly reunited director Stephen Frears, screenwriter Christopher Hampton, and actors John Malkovich and Glenn Close after their work on the Oscar-winning Dangerous Liaisons.",
